      "writtenOn": "2025-07-01T17:25:05Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It is not safe to assume that the EC will initiate an AP boot immediately upon power-up. EC expects to be able to talk to the PDC even while the AP is off (G3). \n\nFor WCL, I decided to forego the GPIO detection and do trial I2C transactions against each of the possible PDC options to see what is installed (https://crrev.com/c/6682245) since all the alternatives (GPIOs, AIC EEPROMs) require S5 and because the cards are interchangeable (which means reading a PDC layout from CBI doesn\u0027t make sense either)",
      "parentUuid": "91b8b451_09287f8c",
